WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.820
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:07.300
Armatos Legio can't be destroyed 
by effects this turn.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:10.800
Then I send Judgment Arrows to the graveyard.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:12.760
What?

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:16.230
He let go of Judgment Arrows?

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:25.140
All faceup cards in your Spell & Trap 
Zone and Main Monster Zone are destroyed!

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:31.240
All his traps are destroyed, so there's 
no way to stop Lightning's monster!

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:32.990
Brother!

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:38.330
Legatus Legionis attacks 
Fortressdrone Beehive!

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:50.970
Blood Shepherd!

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:55.560
I guess I couldn't help you.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:56.680
Me?

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:00.640
It's a brother's responsibility 
to protect his sister.

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:04.610
That's why you acted on your own?

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:07.620
Sorry, Emma.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:11.720
Brother!

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:14.200
Brother?

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:20.870
Blood Shepherd made no mistakes, 
but it defeated him.

00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:25.070
The Light Ignis is a fearsome foe.

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:28.990
Next time, you're up.

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:31.340
Hope you look forward to it.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:54.340
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:55.140 --> 00:02:01.130
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:08.450
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:15.020
Sharing hope for the future

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:21.770
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:29.000
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:35.710
I want to share your pain

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:34.020
I can see the formula 
for victory in any duel.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:37.940
I can no longer lose.

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:46.320
Play...maker...

00:03:47.930 --> 00:03:51.890
His brain and AI's synchronicity 
is still rising!

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:07.770
Brother…

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:17.140
That surprised me.

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:20.480
Ghost Girl and Blood Shepherd were siblings.

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:24.310
He fought Lightning to 
help his sister, but...

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:26.490
How sad.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:30.380
Now that they're apart, I wonder 
if they'll see each other again-

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:38.930
Sorry, Kusanagi.

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:41.090
Don’t worry about me.

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:42.730
Sorry.

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:48.340
In the duel, Blood Shepherd’s strategy 
against Lightning should've worked.

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:52.580
But Lightning anticipated his moves.

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:57.330
AIs naturally anticipate numerous patterns.

00:04:57.330 --> 00:05:02.020
And Lightning is no ordinary AI, 
even though he’s annoying.

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:03.490
Hey, look!

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:10.220
This is…

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:11.660
An Ignis algorithm.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:14.370
The Attribute is… Earth!

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:16.100
Is that Earth?

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:19.840
No way!  Earth is in LINK VRAINS?

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:21.570
Maybe.

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:25.850
What?  But SOL Technologies took Earth.

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:27.340
Maybe he escaped.

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:29.940
For real?

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:32.160
- Hooray!  Hooray!
- But we're not sure yet!

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:32.850
Hoo-

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:36.880
C’mon, just be happy.

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:39.860
How's this possible?

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:42.860
Why do you think negatively?

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:45.690
You’re too carefree.

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:47.720
You’re not happy?

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:50.970
I’m happy if he’s actually safe, but…

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:58.210
Hold up!  If Earth escaped, 
SOL will try to recapture him.

00:05:58.210 --> 00:06:02.920
Not just SOL.  Lightning may also come.

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:03.960
Wanna go?

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:04.920
Yeah.

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:07.410
Deck…

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:08.460
Set!

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:10.620
Into the VRAINS!

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:15.120
Playmaker and Soulburner?

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:17.660
They just appeared in LINK VRAINS.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:21.170
I wonder if they found a lead on Lightning.

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:27.090
I’m going to LINK VRAINS.

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:28.310
Something…

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:29.980
Huh?  What's wrong?

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:31.680
I don’t know, but…

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:32.820
Something...

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:34.320
Something?

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:38.560
Something sad may happen.

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:42.780
Playmaker’s team has 
appeared in LINK VRAINS.

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:44.020
Yes.

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:46.880
Are you planning to send Go Onizuka?

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:53.770
Now that Blood Shepherd is gone, Onizuka 
is the only one who can fight Playmaker.

00:06:53.770 --> 00:06:55.360
It’s too dangerous.

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:59.220
If you keep sending him as 
is, Go Onizuka’s brain-

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:02.840
No, not just his brain.  He’ll 
be hurt physically too!

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:05.090
I need data.

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:09.540
Go Onizuka is my only game 
piece who can collect it.

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:19.080
I'll use the Ignis’s data and Onizuka’s 
test subject data to grow my company.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:22.800
Go Onizuka has already 
captured the Earth Ignis.

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:25.900
That alone has greatly 
contributed to our company!

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:29.740
That’s why I gave it to him.

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:32.700
Gave?  What do you mean?

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:36.160
No further queries.

00:07:36.160 --> 00:07:38.800
Besides, it’s too late.

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:45.850
He already left for LINK VRAINS.

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:52.020
The signal is coming from that area.

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:55.400
Earth is on one of these floating islands.

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:59.000
Kusanagi, can you pinpoint the location?

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:00.530
Something’s coming!

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:03.850
You mean Earth, right?

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:06.610
Earth!  I knew you were okay!

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:09.330
Jump into my arms!

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:12.340
Don’t jump into my arms!

00:08:17.770 --> 00:08:19.020
That’s…

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:23.490
Found you, Playmaker.

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.960
Go Onizuka.

00:08:29.220 --> 00:08:30.920
Ryoken.

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:33.410
Trouble has arrived.

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:37.760
Show me your strength.

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:42.000
Playmaker, I'll end things with you today.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.400
No way...

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:46.620
His face and aura are totally 
different than before.

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:48.980
Is that really Go Onizuka?

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:53.220
By implanting an AI chip in his 
brain, he's been assimilated.

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:55.700
He took Earth.

00:08:55.700 --> 00:09:00.420
SOL is also pursuing Earth, 
so they sent Go Onizuka.

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:04.930
After I take care of Playmaker, 
I’ll take you on.

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:06.410
Wait patiently.

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:12.410
Ai, he already believes that you'll lose.

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:14.010
What a joke!

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:17.100
He’s the one who's going to lose!

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:19.610
Give back Earth!

00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:21.520
Let’s go, Playmaker!

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:23.660
Wait, Go Onizuka!

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:26.090
I don’t want to fight you!

00:09:26.090 --> 00:09:28.220
What are you talking about?

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:31.220
You want to run away now?

00:09:31.220 --> 00:09:35.120
This isn’t the time for 
humans to fight each other!

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:37.200
A huge threat is coming!

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:41.440
He’s no longer the same Onizuka as before!

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:43.250
Go Onizuka!

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:46.400
Fight alongside me, like 
during the Tower of Hanoi!

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:49.400
I need your help!

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:54.380
You defeated the opponent who defeated me.

00:09:54.380 --> 00:09:58.500
Huh?  What’s he suddenly talking about?

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:00.060
He means Revolver.

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:02.740
He’s still obsessed about that?

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:04.720
He can’t let it go.

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:09.730
I was able to defeat Revolver because 
you uncovered what card he had.

00:10:09.730 --> 00:10:12.460
I couldn’t have won on my own!

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:15.260
That’s right.  He had me-

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:15.980
Be quiet!

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:16.900
Okay.

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:24.610
After I lost to you, my 
gears began to malfunction.

00:10:24.610 --> 00:10:31.520
The more I tried to stop them from 
malfunctioning, the more I deteriorated and fell.

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:39.260
And I realized that to climb out 
of the pit, I had to defeat you.

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:42.050
Stop behaving like a child!

00:10:42.050 --> 00:10:42.690
Be quiet!

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:43.890
Okay.

00:10:43.890 --> 00:10:46.730
Even Go Onizuka said that to me.

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:49.920
Are you really not the same as before?

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:56.040
Is Go Onizuka - the proud fighter 
and duelist - really gone?

00:10:56.040 --> 00:11:00.920
I used to be a proud duelist.

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:04.490
When I defeat you, I can be that again!

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:10.220
I'll crush you and climb 
to great heights again.

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:13.880
No matter what they say, he won’t listen.

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:15.460
Go Onizuka…

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:20.450
Seems I have no choice 
but to fight, Go Onizuka.

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:25.680
That’s right.  And this 
will be your final duel!

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:32.540
Speed Duel!

00:11:40.480 --> 00:11:43.880
I’m going max from the start!

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:48.890
Expanding thought capabilities!

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:51.840
Brain Hack Overlimit!

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:58.050
My turn.

00:11:58.050 --> 00:12:00.690
I set a monster.

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:03.300
I end my turn.

00:12:03.300 --> 00:12:06.290
He used the same move against Earth.

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:11.760
His duel will begin when 
I attack his set monster.

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:14.540
Hey, isn’t that Playmaker?

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:15.900
He’s dueling.

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:16.910
Seriously?

00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:19.210
His opponent is Go Onizuka!

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:20.760
That’s Onizuka?

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:21.840
He looks worn out.

00:12:23.020 --> 00:12:24.340
Flame!

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:29.010
Looks like it started.

00:12:29.010 --> 00:12:30.330
Yeah.

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:35.740
I can’t believe that’s Go Onizuka.

00:12:35.740 --> 00:12:38.740
I used to admire him.

00:12:38.740 --> 00:12:43.210
As the hero who saved LINK 
VRAINS with Playmaker.

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:47.680
Tenacity can help raise 
people to new heights.

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:53.920
But it can also go wrong, 
like with my father.

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:56.940
His Anti Skill is a problem.

00:12:56.940 --> 00:12:59.570
He can use it to stop our Skill.

00:12:59.570 --> 00:13:00.160
Yeah.

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:02.800
My turn!  I draw!

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:04.890
I set this card!

00:13:04.890 --> 00:13:07.600
I Special Summon Linkslayer!

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:14.540
When there are no monsters on my field, 
I can Special Summon it from my hand!

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:17.560
Then I summon Storm Cipher!

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:25.760
Since I summoned a Cyberse, I Special 
Summon Boot Staggered from my hand!

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:31.200
He has three monsters with at least 2000 ATK.

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:33.640
He’s planning to end this instantly.

00:13:33.640 --> 00:13:37.250
He doesn't want to give 
Onizuka time to think.

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:38.200
Battle!

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:41.540
Storm Cipher attacks your monster!

00:13:41.540 --> 00:13:45.600
My monster is Dinowrestler Valeonyx.

00:13:49.650 --> 00:13:55.130
I send Dinowrestler Martial Anga from my 
hand to the graveyard to activate its effect!

00:13:55.130 --> 00:14:01.290
Valeonyx can’t be destroyed in battle 
against a monster with equal or greater ATK.

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:05.700
Then it ends the battle.

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:08.920
What?  Not just destruction?

00:14:08.920 --> 00:14:11.920
It also ends the battle.

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:16.420
Playmaker’s strategy was to defeat 
him quickly, but he avoided it.

00:14:17.450 --> 00:14:19.400
I end my turn.

00:14:19.970 --> 00:14:22.770
Why are you trying to end this quickly?

00:14:22.770 --> 00:14:25.340
Are you scared of me?

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:27.880
I’m not scared of you-

00:14:28.580 --> 00:14:31.810
Oh my!  He’s scary!

00:14:31.810 --> 00:14:35.570
Playmaker, you're scared of me.

00:14:35.570 --> 00:14:38.900
Of my thinking ability and my Anti Skill.

00:14:38.900 --> 00:14:41.960
His personality is twisted.

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:45.940
Dinowrestler Martial Anga’s effect 
activates from my graveyard.

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:49.200
When this card uses its effect, 
at the end of the turn...

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:55.450
...when you have more monsters than me, it 
Special Summons itself from the graveyard.

00:14:57.940 --> 00:15:01.960
How boring.  Everything 
is within expectations.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:06.780
Playmaker, I’m talking about your dueling.

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:11.450
Your duel defeated me and 
disrupted everything.

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:14.440
Entertain me more.

00:15:14.440 --> 00:15:17.410
Only you can push me to great heights.

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:20.890
I must defeat you.

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:24.380
I think he's more dangerous than before.

00:15:24.380 --> 00:15:27.380
My turn.  I draw.

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:32.250
Appear!  The circuit to victory!

00:15:32.250 --> 00:15:35.460
The summoning conditions 
are two Dinowrestlers.

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:36.850
Link Summon!

00:15:36.850 --> 00:15:42.500
Appear, Link 2 Dinowrestler Terra Parkourio!

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:49.360
Hey hey.  With only 1000 ATK, it 
stands no chance against our monster.

00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:50.520
Don’t get impatient.

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:54.290
I activate the spell card, Mad Evolution!

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:57.960
I can Special Summon a Dinowrestler

00:15:57.960 --> 00:16:04.440
from my hand in defense position 
whose Level is the same as yours!

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:11.370
Your Storm Cipher is Level 4, so I Special 
Summon Level 4 Dinowrestler Systegosaur!

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:14.890
Systegosaur’s effect activates!

00:16:14.890 --> 00:16:22.500
When it’s Special Summoned, I can add 
World Dino Wrestling from my deck to my hand.

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:25.370
And after Mad Evolution activates...

00:16:25.370 --> 00:16:32.620
...all my monsters become the same Type as 
the target monster until the end of the turn.

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:37.090
Why did he make his cards Cyberse-Type?

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:41.280
What’s wrong?

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:45.760
This sensation…  Can it be?

00:16:48.490 --> 00:16:51.460
Here comes the main event, Playmaker!

00:16:52.930 --> 00:16:55.980
Appear!  The circuit to victory!

00:16:55.980 --> 00:16:59.140
The summoning conditions are two Cyberses!

00:17:04.010 --> 00:17:06.080
Link Summon!

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:08.620
Appear, Link 2...

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:09.730
That’s…

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:15.880
That’s…

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:17.620
What?

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:20.690
Crystal Heart?

00:17:22.730 --> 00:17:24.760
Why?

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:29.460
No way!

00:17:29.460 --> 00:17:33.940
Unbelievable.  Go Onizuka 
has that Ignis’s card?

00:17:35.130 --> 00:17:36.360
Can it be?

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:39.050
Hey!  That’s Earth’s card!

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:40.840
Why do you have it?

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:44.510
Say something!

00:17:44.510 --> 00:17:47.770
How did you get it?  Answer me!

00:17:47.770 --> 00:17:51.160
It's not important how I acquired it.

00:17:51.160 --> 00:17:53.000
It’s how I’ll use it.

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:56.000
You punk…

00:17:56.000 --> 00:18:02.010
There's something different about that 
Crystal Heart than the one Earth used.

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:10.000
Yeah.  It is different.

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:13.120
It’s like it’s turned into Onizuka.

00:18:13.120 --> 00:18:16.340
Yeah.  I sense it's the same as Go Onizuka.

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:19.840
No way!  Onizuka, did you...

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:21.690
That’s right.

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:28.760
Earth…

00:18:28.760 --> 00:18:32.540
They put the Earth Ignis’s 
data into Go Onizuka.

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:37.010
That is something SOL would do.

00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:44.680
The Ignis data is in the AI chip?

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:45.930
Y-Yes.

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:50.140
Just putting an AI chip inside 
a human's brain is very risky!

00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:54.040
But on top of that, you 
put in Ignis data?  Why?

00:18:54.050 --> 00:18:55.600
I ordered so.

00:18:56.120 --> 00:18:59.370
I told you.  I need data.

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:03.380
And I utilize all data effectively.

00:19:03.380 --> 00:19:06.580
And you're willing to do anything?

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:08.100
Exactly.

00:19:09.570 --> 00:19:13.320
Business is about efficiency and production.

00:19:13.320 --> 00:19:15.300
That's the basic of basics.

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:25.020
Earth’s data is in that human.

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:27.490
So due to SOL, Earth really was…

00:19:27.490 --> 00:19:29.690
Damn!

00:19:30.720 --> 00:19:34.770
So the Earth signal we followed was...

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:37.720
A trap to lure us.

00:19:37.720 --> 00:19:39.860
Exactly.

00:19:39.860 --> 00:19:41.500
Stop messing around!

00:19:41.500 --> 00:19:45.490
The Ignis is under my control.

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:47.450
Under your control?

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:51.050
They say you Ignis are a threat to humanity.

00:19:51.050 --> 00:19:54.890
But it’s not bad if 
you’re under my control.

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:59.890
Playmaker!  I've surpassed you!

00:19:59.890 --> 00:20:02.680
Hey.  Let’s definitely crush him.

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:05.440
Keep talking, Dark Ignis.

00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:08.320
You're next to be put under my control.

00:20:08.320 --> 00:20:09.610
I refuse!

00:20:09.610 --> 00:20:14.100
Dinowrestler Terra Parkourio’s 
effect activates from the graveyard!

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:17.560
When it's used to Link Summon 
and sent to the graveyard...

00:20:17.560 --> 00:20:22.810
...I can Special Summon a Dinowrestler 
from my graveyard by negating its effects!

00:20:22.810 --> 00:20:25.490
Come, Martial Anga!

00:20:27.090 --> 00:20:30.490
Crystal Heart’s effect activates.

00:20:30.490 --> 00:20:38.010
It Special Summons and co-links with an 
Earth Link Monster from my graveyard.

00:20:38.010 --> 00:20:40.220
Come, Terra Parkourio!

00:20:42.650 --> 00:20:48.450
When this effect is used, I place 
a G Golem Counter on Crystal Heart.

00:20:48.450 --> 00:20:56.530
For each G Golem Counter, the Earth 
monster next to its link gains 600 ATK!

00:20:57.340 --> 00:21:00.940
He’s using Crystal Heart masterfully.

00:21:00.940 --> 00:21:05.180
I activate the Field Spell, 
World Dino Wrestling!

00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:08.850
Terra Parkourio’s effect activates!

00:21:08.850 --> 00:21:14.900
When World Dino Wrestling activates, I add 
a Dinowrestler in my graveyard to my hand.

00:21:14.900 --> 00:21:17.120
Come, Valeonyx!

00:21:19.120 --> 00:21:20.060
Here it comes!

00:21:20.060 --> 00:21:22.780
Appear!  The circuit to victory!

00:21:22.780 --> 00:21:26.200
The summoning conditions are 
two or more Dinowrestlers!

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:31.520
I set Martial Anga and Link 2 Terra 
Parkourio in the Link Markers!

00:21:33.730 --> 00:21:35.510
Link Summon!

00:21:35.510 --> 00:21:42.760
Appear, Link 3 Dinowrestler King T Wrextle!

00:21:53.900 --> 00:21:59.840
I’ll enjoy this final duel between us.

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:23.900
Trapped in conventionality

00:22:23.900 --> 00:22:25.340
Even denials are obvious

00:22:25.340 --> 00:22:26.470
That There This Whichever

00:22:26.470 --> 00:22:28.310
Hey, isn't it true?

00:22:28.640 --> 00:22:29.970
Why is it before you wake up

00:22:29.970 --> 00:22:31.540
You build a wall, saying it's impossible

00:22:31.540 --> 00:22:32.710
No discussions, no ideals

00:22:37.030 --> 00:22:39.750
Even together, it's not the same

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:42.820
Break yourself through  go way

00:22:43.020 --> 00:22:45.960
Even if you lose your 
way, keep moving forward

00:22:46.290 --> 00:22:49.030
Our desires won't be stopped

00:22:54.400 --> 00:22:57.600
Let your emotions spill

00:22:57.870 --> 00:23:03.740
Keep rewriting  only glory

00:23:04.140 --> 00:23:09.150
If we're together

00:23:09.450 --> 00:23:12.550
We can seize it

00:23:35.920 --> 00:23:42.810
After giving up everything, Onizuka's 
skills rival Playmaker's.

00:23:42.810 --> 00:23:47.680
But emotional strength is 
the determining factor.

00:23:47.680 --> 00:23:53.480
Whether you can believe in yourself 
separates victory from defeat.

00:23:53.480 --> 00:23:56.420
I bet on my instincts!

00:23:56.420 --> 00:24:02.000
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
What's Beyond Instincts

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:04.920
Into the VRAINS!
